[1) The Planning Authority may, with the approval of the Minister, any area to be a planning area for the purposes of this Order.

(2) The Planning Authority shall, in so far as he has not already done so, survey of any planning area to examine the matters that may affect the or the planning of the development, of that area, and shall in any keep all those matters under review.

(3) Notwithstanding that the Planning Authority has carried out his duty subsection (1), the Planning Authority may, if he thinks fits, and shall, if to do so by the Minister, institute a fresh survey of the planning area, the matters that may affect the development, or the planning of the of that area.

(4) prejudice to the generality of subsections (2) and (3), the to be examined and kept under review under those subsections shall

(a) the principal physical, economic, environmental, and social characteristics, including the principal land uses, of the area and, so far as they may be expected to affect that area, those of the neighbouring areas;

(b) the size, composition, and distribution of the population, of that area, whether resident or not;

(c) without prejudice to paragraph (a), the communications, transport and traffic of that area and, so far as they may be expected to affect that area, those of the neighbouring areas;

(d) any matters not mentioned in paragraphs (a}, (b) or (c) that may be expected to affect any matters so mentioned;

(e) such other matters as may be prescribed or as the Minister may in any particular case specify; {(} any changes already projected in any of the matters mentioned in {a}, {b) {c), {d) or {e) and the effect that those changes are likely to have on the development, or the planning of the development, of the area. Preparation of draft Master Plan

(1) The Planning Authority shall, within such period from the of this Order as the Minister may specify, prepare and submit to the Minister a report of his survey under section 8 and at the same time prepare and submit to the Minister for his approval a draft Master Plan complying with

(3).

(2) The report shall include an estimate of any changes likely to occur, such period as the Minister may specify, in the matters mentioned in 8(4) and different periods may be specified in relation to different matters.

(3) The draft Master Plan shall consist of a map and a written statement - {a) formulating the policy and general proposals of the Planning in respect of the development and use of land in the planning area, including measures for the improvement of the physical living communications and the management of traffic;

(b) stating the relationship of those proposals to general proposals for the development and use of land in the neighbouring areas that may be to affect that area; and {c) containing diagrams, illustrations, descriptive matter and such as the Planning Authority thinks fit for the purpose of explaining or the proposals in the plan, or as may be prescribed, or as may in any particular case be specified in directions given by the Minister; and the illustrations, and descriptive matter shall be treated as forming part of the plan.

(4) In formulating his policy and general proposals under subsection j3){a), the Planning Authority shall have regard to{a) the results of his survey under section 8 and by any other that he may obtain;

(b) current policies in respect of the social and economic planning and and the environmental protection of the nation;

(c) the resources likely to be available for the carrying out of the of the Master Plan; and {d/ such other matters as the Minister may direct him to take into

(5) The general proposals of the Planning Authority under this section in of land, shall indicate any part of the planning area that he has selected for the commencement of comprehensive treatment during a prescribed period, in accordance with a District Plan and a Local Plan prepared for the selected area by development, redevelopment, or improvement, or partly by one and partly by another method, of the whole or part of the area selected, and the nature of the treatment selected.

(6) When the Minister approves a proposal for the development and use of land under this Order, such approved proposal shall have effect and prevail over any special conditions which may be entered in the Register under section 9(5) of the Land Code (Chapter 40) in respect of any title issued under section 3 or 6 of the Code. in connection with preparation of draft Master Plan

(1) The Planning Authority, in the course of preparing a draft Master Plan or a draft District Plan or before the Minister approves or rejects a draft Master Plan or a draft District Plan, may, if he thinks it desirable, prepare a draft Local Plan for any part of the local area.

(2) the Master Plan or the District Plan has come into effect, the Authority shall consider, and thereafter keep under review, the of preparing and, if he considers it desirable and he has not already done so, shall prepare a draft Local Plan for any part or for the whole of the local area.

(3) A draft Local Plan shall consist of maps and written statements and {a) formulate, in such details as the Planning Authority thinks fit, other things, his proposals for -

(i) the development of;

(ii) the use of land in;

(iii) the protection and improvement of the physical environment of;

(iv) the preservation of the natural topography of;

(v) the improvement of the landscape of;

(vi) the preservation and planting of trees in;

(vii) the making up of open spaces in;

(viii) the preservation and enhancement of character and of buildings in;

(ix) the designation of conservation area in;

(x) the improvement of communications in;

(xi) the improvement of infrastructure in;

(xii) the management of traffic in; or

(xiii) the land readjustment scheme in, the area of the plans; (b} contain diagrams, illustrations, descriptive matter and such other as the Planning Authority thinks fit for the purpose of explaining or the proposals in the plans, or as may be prescribed, or as may in any particular case be specified in directions given by Minister; and the diagrams, illustrations, descriptive matter shall be treated as forming part of the plan.·

(4) If an area is indicated as an action area in the Master Plan or the District Plan, the Planning Authority shall, if he has not already done so, after the Master Plan or the District Plan comes into effect, prepare a draft Local Plan for that area.

(5) prejudice to subsections (1) to (3), the Planning Authority shall, if the Minister gives him a direction in respect of a part of an area for which a Master Plan or a draft District Plan has been, or is in the course of being, as soon as practicable prepare for that part a draft Local Plan of such nature as may be specified in the direction.

(6) under subsection (5) may be given by the Minister either or after the draft Master Plan or the draft District Plan comes into effect.

(7) In formulating his proposals in a draft Local Plan, the Planning shall secure that the proposals conform generally to the Master Plan or the District Plan as it stands for the time being, whether or not it has come into and shall have regard to any information and other considerations that to him to be relevant, or that may be prescribed, or that the Minister may in any particular case direct him to take into account.

(8) When the Minister approves a proposal for the development and use of land under this Order, such approved proposal shall have effect and prevail over any special conditions which may be entered in the Register under section 9(5) of the Land Code (Chapter 40) in respect of any title issued under section 3 or 6 of the Code.

(9) For the purposes of subsection [4), "action area" means the area selected for the commencement of comprehensive treatment under section 9(5) or 13(5). in connection with preparation of draft Local Plan

